title: Expanding Healthcare
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; coalition_affairs_timer = 5
view-if: dems_in_government = 1 
card-image: img/muller_cabinet.jpg

= Coalition Affairs

Our coalition is in trouble. The right-leaning members of the Center [? if in_grand_coalition: and DVP ?] are constantly criticizing us for our policies, and are threatening to call a vote of no confidence to collapse this government[? if spd_prussia :, or to do the same for our government in the state of Prussia ?].

How do we reduce tensions with the coalition?

- @use_section_1115: Approve medicaid expansions
- @crack_down_on_overpayments: Crackdown on medicare advantage fraud
- @healthcare_legislation: Go to legislative options
- @easy_discard


@use_section_1115
subtitle: Provisions in Medicaid allow us to approve of "experimental" healthcare coverage by other states. This has historically been used to help lower income mothers the most.
choose-if: medicare_for_all = 0
max-visits: 2
unavailable=subtitle: Our previous healthcare reforms makes this irrelevant. 
on-arrival: {!
Q.progressive_dissent -=3
Q.socialist_dissent -=3
Q.healthcare_cost_progress +=3
Q.nat_support.age.mid +=2
Q.nat_support.inc.low +=2
Q.nat_support.inc.high -=1
window.simulate_polling();
!}

Fine. By cutting welfare, we have reduced dissent within the coalition.

@crack_down_on_overpayments
subtitle: +0.40 budget. Insurers are attempting to make seniors look sicker then they actually are to reciece higher government payouts. These practices cost the government money and make healthcare more expensive for everyone
view-if: historical_mode = 0
maximum-visits: 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget +=0.4
Q.socialist_dissent -=3
Q.healthcare_cost_progress +=3
Q.nat_support.age.senior +=3
Q.corporate_backlash +=1
window.simulate_polling();
!}

By transferring campaign funds to our coalition partners, we can make our policies more acceptable to them. Some would call this corruption, but perhaps it is necessary to save democracy.

@no_change

No. We will not do this.

@bring_down
subtitle: Bring down this government before our opponents do.
on-arrival: dems_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; in_weimar_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; spd_toleration = 0; socialist_strength += 8; pro_republic -= 5; new_middle_spd -= 3; rural_spd -= 3; old_middle_spd -= 3; catholics_spd -= 3; blue_dog_dissent += 5

We have called for a vote of no confidence in ourselves, and have brought down this government. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] currently rules as acting chancellor.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

